        <body>
            <div xml:id="d42">

                <pb facs="0144" n="60" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg60"/>

                <head>No. 41.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Hall.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-04-21"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 21,
                        1886</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 341.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 480, of the 19th
                    ultimo, concerning the convention signed at Amapala, January 13, 1886,
                    re-establishing amicable relations between Nicaragua and Salvador, and have to
                    say that the same has been read with friendly interest in what touches the
                    assured peace of the sister Republics of Central America.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
